::JOUR_U04_L05_GP_Q01::[MLA.JOUR.MED.05] Source: Title: The Quiet Work Before Opening Night. Intro: The auditorium is dim except for the blue glow of the stage lights. A ladder leans beside the curtain, scripts rest open on the front row, and a student sweeps sawdust from the edge of the set. Caption 1: Behind the bright posters and applause, the stage crew builds a small world from tape, paint, and patient hands. Caption 2: The empty seats wait in silence while the cast repeats the final scene for the fifth time. Caption 3: By Friday night, the nervous quiet will become music, movement, and a room full of voices. Design note: The package uses low-light photographs, close-up images of hands and tools, and short captions to create a reflective mood about preparation. Question 1: Which mood is best supported by the source? {
